{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1521294-post-apocalyptic-hunter-campaign-idea","id":1521294,"title":"Post Apocalyptic Hunter Campaign Idea","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-08-23T15:55:41-07:00","id":1521294,"title":"Post Apocalyptic Hunter Campaign Idea","content":"This campaign is set in a fairly typical post-apocalyptic setting Ala Golden Age Sci Fi. However, it is the <b>WoD</b> that collapsed. The survivors face brutal extra challenges. <br /> <br /> The Imbued Hunters in this setting had an offer made to them. They disliked being offered a deal by the witches and wizards, but they didn't have much choice. <br /> <br /> The PCs in this Campaign are Imbued Hunters disguised as peddlers. The magic users (they like to be called Mages) provide the Hunters trade goods. The Hunters are given the means and cover to continue the hunt. And Vampires are out there and other strange things. The mages get the Hunters as a means to work on restoring society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-23T16:11:22-07:00","id":1521295,"title":"","content":"Small groups of Hunters go out as peddlers and show people (the free show is supposed to attract customers to buy the peddler's goods). This gives the Hunters an excuse to travel around the countryside (it's their job). <br /> <br /> Peddlers often get the best gossip. Always a major tool in the hunt. As the Hunters sale vitally needed goods, everyone owes them little favors. <br /> <br /> The &quot;Mages&quot; send out things like high quality seeds, useful hard to make tools, and cheap durable books. These help change conditions. <br /> <br /> Take the seeds. These seeds grow tough plants that are resistant to many ordinary garden hazards. They are also more nutritious than even the best modern crops. The tools and books give people the ability to better their lives.<br /> <br /> The Mages also provide things like coffee, tea, sugar, chocolate, and spices. People think twice before cutting off their chocolate supply. How long could you go without coffee, tea, or sugar. <br /> <br /> The Hunters travel in wagons designed to be mobile markets. As gasoline is no longer widely available, the Hunters use horses.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-23T16:18:21-07:00","id":1521296,"title":"","content":"The Mages (Tradition Mages with allies) have bases were they manufacture or grow the needed goods. These bases are towns the Mages are trying to restore. <br /> <br /> Although Paradox is still around, it is much weaker. Given how low the population is (around 250 million world wide) the difficulties of casting spells are greatly reduced. <br /> <br /> The Hunters realize that the Mages are now more powerful and a greater threat. However the Vampires are starving for blood and the main threat. <br /> <br /> More later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-23T17:49:19-07:00","id":1521300,"title":"","content":"I think you're lost, imbued hunters and tradition mages are world of darkness, this is chronicles of darkness. <br /> <br /> I wouldn't make mages even stronger, mages are generally the strongest thing already. I would say the Apocalypse reinforced reality, not weakened it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-24T02:41:50-07:00","id":1521321,"title":"","content":"A) I did post to the wrong place.<br /> <br /> B) The Mages aren't supposed to be trying to be stronger. It's just the reduced population has that side effect. And the Mages are trying to use what they can get to help people.<br /> <br /> The Ascension Mages would benefit, whereas Awakening Mages wouldn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-24T03:32:00-07:00","id":1521322,"title":"","content":"Ascension Mages would not benefit from the Apocalypse, there's more to consensus than the number of people on Earth. Nephandi would benefit though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-24T15:30:41-07:00","id":1521352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1521294-post-apocalyptic-hunter-campaign-idea?p=1521322#post1521322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ascension Mages would not benefit from the Apocalypse, there's more to consensus than the number of people on Earth. Nephandi would benefit though.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, Mages are inhibited by the presence of large numbers of people. I'll have to find the book but the difficulty of performing magic increased with population. So, although the monstrous deaths caused by the catastrophe sickened all Trad Mages, it reduced the difficulty of magic. <br /> <br /> Second, the population is simply to low and dispersed to support Paradox at anything like precatastrophe levels. <br /> <br /> The Council Mages and other surviving non Nephandi didn't want the catastrophe but it has reduced their difficulties. It has also taken away humanity's hopes and opportunities. The Hunters in this setting are allied with the Mages to help humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-24T22:09:56-07:00","id":1521363,"title":"","content":"Shouldn't this be moved to the world of darkness forums now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-25T00:23:22-07:00","id":1521364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1521294-post-apocalyptic-hunter-campaign-idea?p=1521363#post1521363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shouldn't this be moved to the world of darkness forums now?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm reposting. If we all just ignore this thread, it will go away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}